      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $3+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}$ for $t>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(3+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(3+\\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= 3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t+\\int t^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= 3\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{t^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\ &= 3t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
